{
  "case_id": "2007-06-694",
  "document_hash": "f22ed9248edc2d65f02d3b1e2f12bd07722b72fda05629ff99e65bb729cd7233",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2007-06-694",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f22ed9248edc2d65f02d3b1e2f12bd07722b72fda05629ff99e65bb729cd7233",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f22ed9248edc-0000-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: We'll hear argument first this morning in case 06-694, United States v. Williams."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (United States)",
      "case_id": "2007-06-694",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f22ed9248edc2d65f02d3b1e2f12bd07722b72fda05629ff99e65bb729cd7233",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f22ed9248edc-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "This Court has made clear that speech proposing an unlawful transaction is not protected by the First Amendment.\nAnd speech that falsely proposes an unlawful transaction is likewise unprotected."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2007-06-694",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f22ed9248edc2d65f02d3b1e2f12bd07722b72fda05629ff99e65bb729cd7233",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f22ed9248edc-0000-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 10,
        "start": 10
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOUTER: That's -- that's fine, but before you get to that point, you have -- there's still an indictable offense."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2007-06-694",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f22ed9248edc2d65f02d3b1e2f12bd07722b72fda05629ff99e65bb729cd7233",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f22ed9248edc-0000-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 16,
        "start": 16
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: I just wanted to clarify the footnote to which the Chief referred, that footnote 4 in your reply brief. It says, to the contrary, the government's brief expressly acknowledges that the statute's proscription encompasses noncommercial speech."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2007-06-694",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "f22ed9248edc2d65f02d3b1e2f12bd07722b72fda05629ff99e65bb729cd7233",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f22ed9248edc-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Even though -- even though what you are, in fact, showing or presenting does not fit the definition? Even if what you're showing -- you say, have I got some hot child porn and here it is, and the \"it\" is -- is -- an adult pretending to be a child, or a virtual image."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Clement",
      "case_id": "2007-06-694",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "f22ed9248edc2d65f02d3b1e2f12bd07722b72fda05629ff99e65bb729cd7233",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f22ed9248edc-0001-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "GENERAL CLEMENT: That's right, Justice Ginsburg. If the scienter requirements are satisfied and I'm consciously trying to get you to believe that even though I have something that for some technical reason is not the real thing, what I'm offering you is the real thing, the statute does target that."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2007-06-694",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "f22ed9248edc2d65f02d3b1e2f12bd07722b72fda05629ff99e65bb729cd7233",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f22ed9248edc-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOUTER: But how would you do it in the case -- you mentioned that if there is not actual child porn shown, and there is a truthful or honest statement about it, that there is nothing to worry about."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2007-06-694",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "f22ed9248edc2d65f02d3b1e2f12bd07722b72fda05629ff99e65bb729cd7233",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f22ed9248edc-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Do we use a seven year old for the objective requirement?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2007-06-694",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "f22ed9248edc2d65f02d3b1e2f12bd07722b72fda05629ff99e65bb729cd7233",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f22ed9248edc-0001-0006",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 29,
        "start": 29
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "ORAL ARGUMENT OF RICHARD J. DIAZ ON BEHALF OF RESPONDENT"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Richard J. Diaz",
      "case_id": "2007-06-694",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "f22ed9248edc2d65f02d3b1e2f12bd07722b72fda05629ff99e65bb729cd7233",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f22ed9248edc-0001-0007",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 29
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "carries a 5-year mandatory minimum prison term and a possible 20-year prison term"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2007-06-694",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f22ed9248edc2d65f02d3b1e2f12bd07722b72fda05629ff99e65bb729cd7233",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f22ed9248edc-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: Suppose we did this? What would you think about an opinion, and why, which says the following? We take every one of those examples and all the ones listed here and put them in appendix A, and the opinion says this is the Solicitor General's interpretation of the statute, as amended, say with the word presentment, which comes out of promotion infer, and we think under that interpretation of the statute, none of these things, nor anything like them, could be prosecuted."
    },
